+
+Numeric constant-buffer reads may precede a source branch when the entry's AIR parameter
+explicitly declares `readonly dereferenceable(n)` in constant address space 2. The entire
+load must fit that byte span, and its offset and parameter alignment must satisfy the
+load alignment. The native typed-IR transform moves the read and constant address path
+before interface construction; its dominating value therefore survives ordinary source
+proof serialization without additional safety metadata. Helper-only promises, volatile
+or atomic reads, loaded resource pointers, dynamic offsets and merely `NonWritable`
+storage loads do not authorize this transformation. Cache identities must change;
+reflection 66, source-proof version 2 and argument-table ABI 9 remain unchanged.
